        -- Questions for Test 7
Today has been one of the most fulfilling days of my life. Three weeks ago, I found a tiny golden puppy shivering near our society gate with a badly injured paw. Seeing his terrified whimper, I couldn''t walk away. With Dr. Verma''s medical help, we cleaned the wound, administered antibiotics, and nurtured him back to health on our porch. Today, our compassionate neighbor, Mrs. Sen, officially adopted him and named him ''Sheru''. Watching Sheru wag his tail joyfully and nuzzle into his new warm bed brought tears to my eyes. Small acts of kindness possess enormous power to heal broken lives. I go to sleep with a heart brimming with peace.
Goodnight,
Anmol', '2 Marks for format (Day, Date, Salutation) and voice; 2 Marks for narrative coherence and emotional depth; 1 Mark for mechanics', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
