        VALUES
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Based on the reading passage, answer: (i) What metaphor does the author use to describe the water-regulating function of forests? (ii) Explain how deforestation accelerates river siltation and flooding. (iii) Find a word from the passage that means ''arid or lacking sufficient moisture''.', NULL, NULL, 'CASE', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 10, '(i) The author uses the metaphor of ''giant green sponges'' to illustrate how forests absorb, store, and gradually release rainwater. (ii) When tree cover is destroyed, heavy rainfall strikes unprotected topsoil directly, dislodging dirt and carrying sediment down into riverbeds, which reduces water-carrying capacity and causes flooding. (iii) The word is ''arid''.', '1 Mark for metaphor identification; 2 Marks for deforestation siltation mechanism; 1 Mark for vocabulary synonym', 'Ecosystems across our planet depend on delicate ecological balances. Forests act as giant green sponges, soaking up rainwater during wet spells, replenishing underground aquifers, and gradually releasing water throughout arid dry seasons. When hillsides are denuded through deforestation, torrential downpours wash away fertile topsoil into river channels, silting reservoirs and causing destructive flash floods in lower plains. Preserving indigenous old-growth biodiversity is not merely an aesthetic choice, but an ecological necessity for sustainable human survival.', NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 'Refer to the text and answer: (i) How do adaptive learning platforms cater to individual learners according to the passage? (ii) What crucial pedagogical dimensions remain outside the capability of artificial algorithms? (iii) Give the antonym of ''uniform'' as used in the context.', NULL, NULL, 'CASE', 'English', 'Reading Comprehension', 10, '(i) Adaptive platforms use diagnostic algorithms to measure response times, pinpoint misconceptions, and customize instructional scaffolding to each student''s pace. (ii) Human emotional intelligence, peer empathy, moral values, and nuanced creative debates cannot be automated. (iii) Antonym: ''Divergent'', ''varied'', or ''customized''.', '1.5 Marks for adaptive system capabilities; 1.5 Marks for human affective aspects; 1 Mark for contextual antonym', 'Artificial Intelligence and digital computing have reshaped the learning landscape. Traditional classrooms relied heavily on uniform teacher-led pacing, often leaving divergent learners struggling or bored. Adaptive learning platforms utilize diagnostic algorithms to measure student response times, identify cognitive misconceptions, and tailor instructional scaffolding to individual needs. However, educational psychologists emphasize that emotional intelligence, peer empathy, moral compass, and creative debate cannot be replicated by silicon processors.', NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 'Fill in the blank with the correct determiner: ''There wasn''t _______ milk left in the refrigerator, so we couldn''t make tea.''', '{"A":"much","B":"many","C":"few","D":"several"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Determiners', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, '''Milk'' is an uncountable noun, so the quantifier ''much'' is grammatically appropriate with the negative verb.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000004', 'Choose the correct modal to complete the sentence: ''You _______ submit your project dossier before 5:00 PM today, as late submissions are rejected.''', '{"A":"must","B":"might","C":"could","D":"would"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Modals', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, '''Must'' expresses strong obligation and strict official necessity.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000005', 'Subject-Verb Concord: ''Neither the principal nor the teachers _______ present at the venue when the storm hit.''', '{"A":"was","B":"were","C":"is","D":"are"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Subject-Verb Concord', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'With correlative conjunctions ''neither...nor'', the verb agrees with the nearer subject (''teachers'', which is plural).', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000006', 'Reported Speech: Rahul said, ''I have finished my science experiment.'' The indirect speech is:', '{"A":"Rahul said that he had finished his science experiment.","B":"Rahul said that he has finished his science experiment.","C":"Rahul told that he finished his science experiment.","D":"Rahul says he has finished his science experiment."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reported Speech', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Present perfect (''have finished'') shifts to past perfect (''had finished'') in indirect speech when reporting verb is in the past.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', 'Fill in the blank with the correct tense: ''By the time the rescue team arrived, the local villagers _______ the injured passengers.''', '{"A":"evacuated","B":"had evacuated","C":"have evacuated","D":"are evacuating"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Tenses', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The past perfect tense (''had evacuated'') denotes the earlier completed action before another past event occurred.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 'You recently visited an old age home with your school voluntary service club. Write a Descriptive Paragraph in about 100-120 words describing your observations, the residents'' emotions, and the impact the visit left on your mind.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Descriptive Paragraph', 5, 'A Visit to the Old Age Home: Last Saturday, our school voluntary club visited ''Sandhya Aashray'', a serene refuge for senior citizens. Walking into the sunny courtyard, we were greeted by silver-haired elders whose eyes reflected both wisdom and an unspoken yearning for companionship. We spent the afternoon singing melodious vintage songs, reciting poetry, and listening to their poignant life journeys. Mrs. Shanti, an eighty-year-old retired teacher, affectionately held my hand while reminiscing about her teaching days. Despite physical frailties, their grace and warm smiles were deeply touching. However, a lingering melancholy pervaded the corridors, revealing the quiet sting of abandonment by their busy families. The experience awakened in me a profound sense of gratitude and reaffirmed that our elders deserve dignity, unconditional love, and constant care.', '2 Marks for content relevance and vivid sensory descriptions; 2 Marks for organization and vocabulary; 1 Mark for grammatical accuracy', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040008-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'Taking inspiration from the theme of empathy and resilience, write a Diary Entry in about 100-120 words expressing your feelings when you helped a stray injured puppy recover and found it a loving home.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Diary Entry', 5, 'Dear Diary,
