        ('90040024-0000-4000-8000-000000000004', 'Reference to Context (Poetry - The Road Not Taken): ''Two roads diverged in a yellow wood, / And sorry I could not travel both / And be one traveler, long I stood / And looked down one as far as I could...'' (i) What do the ''two diverging roads'' symbolize in human life? (ii) Why did the poet choose the second road? (iii) What does the phrase ''yellow wood'' signify?', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'English', 'The Road Not Taken', 6, '(i) The two diverging roads symbolize the inevitable, fateful choices and decisions that every individual must make in the journey of life. (ii) The poet chose the second road because it was grassy, less traveled by the crowd, and ''wanted wear'', representing an unconventional, bold path. (iii) ''Yellow wood'' signifies the autumn season, representing maturity, change, and the passage of time.', '1.5 Marks for symbolical interpretation of roads; 2 Marks for justifying road choice; 1.5 Marks for autumn season significance', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040024-0000-4000-8000-000000000005', 'Short Answer (Beehive): How did Evelyn Glennie achieve her monumental musical success despite losing her hearing ability at a young age? What inspiration does she offer to differently-abled people?', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'The Sound of Music', 10, 'Evelyn Glennie refused to surrender to profound deafness. Guided by percussionist Ron Forbes, she learned to sense acoustic vibrations through different parts of her body rather than her ears—feeling higher drums from the waist up and lower drums from the waist down. Through iron willpower and unremitting practice, she mastered over a thousand percussion instruments and became a celebrated international soloist, proving that physical impairments cannot constrain determination.', '1.5 Marks for Ron Forbes guidance and vibration sensing technique; 1.5 Marks for inspirational message of perseverance', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
